<section image-layout="blank" id="r0J9tXrBlz"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item id="sM-r5cMFcr" background-color="surface" vertical-align="center" colspan="36"><p role="eyebrow">Illustrative program concept · The Restorative Hour</p><h1 font-size="46pt">One hour to make the stay feel different</h1><h3 role="subheading">A hosted in-property ritual helps guests shift from travel mode into the character and pace of the hotel.</h3><grid recipe="process-steps" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item colspan="20"><h4>Arrive</h4><p font-size="16pt">Set down the journey.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="20"><h4>Restore</h4><p font-size="16pt">Follow a guided ritual.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="20"><h4>Return</h4><p font-size="16pt">Re-enter the stay with a memorable story.</p></grid-item></grid><grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item background-color="accent" padding="14pt 16pt"><p font-size="18pt"><b>Manager proposition:</b> pilot the format for six weeks, then continue, adapt, or stop on agreed evidence.</p></grid-item></grid></grid-item><grid-item id="aSGnxK6YxM" padding="0" colspan="24"><ai-image prompt="Observed editorial hospitality photograph inside a distinctive boutique hotel library lounge, an adult guest seated comfortably while a qualified host or practitioner offers a simple choice of tea and journal before a quiet guided restorative ritual, only hands and partial figures visible, tactile white linen and clear glass, soft natural window light, crisp white and sea-glass teal palette with deep teal shadows, generous calm space, welcoming rather than clinical, no yoga pose, no text, no logos" fill="true"></ai-image></grid-item></grid></section>